Reconstructing the active formatting elements across an auto-closed
block boundary -- the canonical reason this algorithm exists (an open
<b> dropped off the stack by <p>'s auto-close must reopen inside the
new block for subsequent content).

#data
<p><b>bold<div>next</div>
#document
| <html>
|   <head>
|   <body>
|     <p>
|       <b>
|         "bold"
|     <div>
|       <b>
|         "next"
